  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade mission on Horticulture to Nigeria 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Agrofood Nigeria Fair is a strategic stepping stone for the newly approved horticultural computed tomography (Horti-CT) in Nigeria. It allows the Netherlands to showcase itself through its private sector and Dutch funded programmes.At the same time, the Dutch government can use the gathering of these actors to discuss and promote its Horti-CT and collect leads for further implementation, with focus on developing of public-private partnerships, like PIB and Impact Clusters, in the horticulture food system in Southwest Nigeria.Through the trade mission the following goals can be achieved within the Horti-CT:1.	Business-to-Business (B2B) cooperation between Dutch and Nigerian small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) is stimulated and strengthened by networking and matchmaking;2.	Focus is on trade and investments that benefit people, create jobs and preferably, are accompanied by the transfer of knowledge and skills;3.	Through business cooperation, the aim is to enhance food and nutritional security in Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
